## 4. Stack

TypeScript end to end, as `00-initial` suggests.

| Piece | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime | Node 22+, `tsx` for running TS directly | No build step for the server in dev |
| HTTP + WS | `express` + `ws` | Boring and well documented |
| MCP | `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (Streamable HTTP transport, **stateless** mode) | Official SDK. Stateless means no session bookkeeping, and every tool call reads the one shared scene |
| Schemas | `zod` | Shared by MCP tool input schemas and WS message validation |
| Editor | Vite + React, rendering **SVG** | The UI will grow panels (palette, notes, variants), and SVG matches the "UI renders to SVG" decision |
| Dev serving | Vite in **middleware mode** inside the server | One process, one port, one command |
| Tests | `vitest` | Only for the scene core in this phase |

**Confirmed:** React for the editor. Port `5170`.

